## Usage Patterns

### Basic Title Topbar

```tsx
<EtTopbar>
  <EtTopbar.Title>Page Title</EtTopbar.Title>
</EtTopbar>
```

### Topbar with Back Navigation

```tsx
<EtTopbar>
  <EtTopbar.Start>
    <EtTopbar.Action accessibilityLabel="Go back" onPress={goBack}>
      <EtoroIcon icon={{ iconName: 'chevronLeft' }} appearance={{ size: 24 }} />
    </EtTopbar.Action>
  </EtTopbar.Start>
  <EtTopbar.Middle>
    <EtTopbar.Title>Settings</EtTopbar.Title>
  </EtTopbar.Middle>
</EtTopbar>
```

### Full Topbar with Multiple Actions

```tsx
<EtTopbar testID="main-topbar">
  <EtTopbar.Start>
    <EtTopbar.Action accessibilityLabel="Go back" onPress={goBack}>
      <EtoroIcon icon={{ iconName: 'chevronLeft' }} appearance={{ size: 24 }} />
    </EtTopbar.Action>
  </EtTopbar.Start>
  <EtTopbar.Middle>
    <EtTopbar.Title>Portfolio</EtTopbar.Title>
  </EtTopbar.Middle>
  <EtTopbar.End>
    <EtTopbar.Action accessibilityLabel="Search" onPress={openSearch}>
      <EtoroIcon icon={{ iconName: 'search' }} appearance={{ size: 24 }} />
    </EtTopbar.Action>
    <EtTopbar.Action accessibilityLabel="Menu" onPress={openMenu}>
      <EtoroIcon icon={{ iconName: 'menu' }} appearance={{ size: 24 }} />
    </EtTopbar.Action>
  </EtTopbar.End>
</EtTopbar>
```

### Implicit Middle Slot

Children not wrapped in a slot component are automatically placed in the middle:

```tsx
// These are equivalent:
<EtTopbar>
  <EtTopbar.Title>Title</EtTopbar.Title>
</EtTopbar>

<EtTopbar>
  <EtTopbar.Middle>
    <EtTopbar.Title>Title</EtTopbar.Title>
  </EtTopbar.Middle>
</EtTopbar>
```

## Component API

### EtTopbar (Root)

Uses regular `View`. For scroll-driven animations, use `EtTopbar.Animated`.

| Prop     | Type                 | Description                |
| -------- | -------------------- | -------------------------- |
| children | ReactNode            | Slot components or content |
| style    | StyleProp<ViewStyle> | Static ViewStyle           |
| testID   | string               | Test identifier            |

### EtTopbar.Animated

Uses `Animated.View` for Reanimated animated styles.

| Prop     | Type                     | Description                                         |
| -------- | ------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------- |
| children | ReactNode                | Slot components or content                          |
| style    | AnimatedStyle<ViewStyle> | Supports both static and Reanimated animated styles |
| testID   | string                   | Test identifier                                     |

### EtTopbar.Start / Middle / End

| Prop         | Type                 | Description                                          |
| ------------ | -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |
| children     | ReactNode            | Slot content                                         |
| style        | StyleProp<ViewStyle> | Custom slot styles                                   |
| testID       | string               | Test identifier                                      |
| ...ViewProps | -                    | All other View props (accessibility, onLayout, etc.) |

### EtTopbar.Action

| Prop               | Type       | Description                        |
| ------------------ | ---------- | ---------------------------------- |
| children           | ReactNode  | Action content (usually icon)      |
| onPress            | () => void | Press handler                      |
| accessibilityLabel | string     | Screen reader label for the action |
| testID             | string     | Test identifier                    |
| hitSlop            | number     | Touch area padding (default: 10)   |
| ...PressableProps  | -          | All Pressable props supported      |

### EtTopbar.Title

| Prop          | Type                 | Description                               |
| ------------- | -------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| children      | ReactNode            | Title text                                |
| variant       | EtTextVariant        | Text variant (default: 'heading-compact') |
| numberOfLines | number               | Line limit (default: 1)                   |
| style         | StyleProp<TextStyle> | Custom text styles                        |
| testID        | string               | Test identifier                           |

## Common Tasks

### Adding a New Slot Type

1. Create the slot component in `subcomponents/`:

   ```typescript
   export function TopbarCustom({ children, style, testID }: ViewProps) {
     return <View style={style} testID={testID}>{children}</View>;
   }
   TopbarCustom.etTopbarSlot = 'custom' as SlotName;
   ```

2. Add to `SlotName` type in `api/types.ts`
3. Add to `SLOT_COMPONENTS` in `hooks/use-slots.ts`
4. Export from `subcomponents/index.ts`
5. Add to `EtTopbar` compound component

### Customizing Topbar Height

Override the `minHeight` in styles:

```tsx
<EtTopbar style={{ minHeight: 80 }}>...</EtTopbar>
```

### Customizing Padding

```tsx
<EtTopbar style={{ paddingHorizontal: 16, paddingVertical: 12 }}>...</EtTopbar>
```

### Scroll-Driven Animations

Use `EtTopbar.Animated` for Reanimated animated styles. The screen owns the scroll state; the topbar is purely presentational.

```tsx
import { useAnimatedStyle, interpolate, useSharedValue, useAnimatedScrollHandler } from 'react-native-reanimated';

function MyScreen() {
  const scrollY = useSharedValue(0);

  const animatedTopbarStyle = useAnimatedStyle(() => ({
    opacity: interpolate(scrollY.value, [0, 100], [1, 0.8]),
    transform: [{ translateY: interpolate(scrollY.value, [0, 100], [0, -64]) }],
  }));

  return (
    <View style={{ flex: 1 }}>
      <EtTopbar.Animated style={animatedTopbarStyle}>
        <EtTopbar.Title>Animated Title</EtTopbar.Title>
      </EtTopbar.Animated>
      <Animated.ScrollView
        onScroll={useAnimatedScrollHandler((event) => {
          scrollY.value = event.contentOffset.y;
        })}
      >
        {/* Content */}
      </Animated.ScrollView>
    </View>
  );
}
```

**Key principle**: Scroll state is managed by the screen, not the topbar. This follows the `patterns-explicit-variants` rule—use the explicit `Animated` variant when you need animation support.

## Slot Distribution Logic

The `useSlots` hook processes children and distributes them into start, middle, and end slots:

1. Iterates through all children
2. Identifies slot components via the `etTopbarSlot` static property (e.g., `TopbarStart.etTopbarSlot = 'start'`)
3. Groups children by slot name (start, middle, end)
4. For each recognized slot component, extracts the following from its props:
   - `children` — the slot's content
   - `style` — custom styles for this slot instance
   - `testID` — test identifier
   - `additionalProps` — all remaining ViewProps (e.g., `accessibilityLabel`, `onLayout`, `pointerEvents`)
5. Collects "loose" children (elements not wrapped in a slot component)
6. Places loose children in middle slot if no explicit `EtTopbar.Middle` content exists
7. Returns slot metadata for start, middle, and end, each containing:
   - `children` — array of collected slot content
   - `styles` — array of collected style objects
   - `testID` — first encountered testID for the slot
   - `additionalProps` — array of collected additional ViewProps

All `additionalProps` are forwarded to the rendered slot Views, allowing full control over accessibility and layout behavior.

## Best Practices for AI Assistants

1. **Use compound components**: Always use `EtTopbar.Start`, `EtTopbar.End`, etc. for slot content
2. **Add testIDs**: Include testID on root and slots for testing
3. **Use EtTopbar.Action**: Wrap interactive elements in Action for consistent hit slop
4. **Set accessibilityLabel**: On Action components for screen reader support
5. **Center titles**: Use `EtTopbar.Middle` or let implicit centering handle it
6. **Check z-index**: Start/end have z-index 2, middle has z-index 1

## Troubleshooting

**Q: Title not centering correctly**
A: Ensure title is in `EtTopbar.Middle` or as a direct child (not in Start/End)

**Q: Action buttons not responding to taps**
A: Check z-index; start/end slots (z-index 2) should be above middle (z-index 1)

**Q: Custom styles not applying**
A: Pass `style` prop to the specific slot component, not just root

**Q: Content overlapping**
A: Middle slot is absolutely positioned; ensure start/end content doesn't overflow

## Liquid Glass (iOS 26+)

EtTopbar automatically detects Liquid Glass availability (iOS 26+) and adapts its rendering:

### Behavior When Liquid Glass Is Active

- **Transparent background**: The topbar root becomes transparent so glass elements float over content.
- **Glass-wrapped slots**: Start and End slot children are automatically wrapped in an `EtGlassView`.
  - **Single child** in a slot → circular glass surface.
  - **Multiple children** in a slot → pill-shaped glass surface.
- **Middle slot**: Not glass-wrapped by the topbar itself. Components placed in Middle (e.g., `EtTextToggle`) handle their own glass treatment via `LiquidGlassContext`.
- **LiquidGlassContext**: Provided by the topbar root. Subcomponents and children can consume it via `useLiquidGlassContext()` from `etoro-ui/core`.

### Behavior When Liquid Glass Is Unavailable (Android, iOS < 26)

- Rendering is identical to the pre-Liquid-Glass design. No visual change.
- `GlassSlotWrapper` renders children directly without any wrapper.

### Infrastructure Used

- `useLiquidGlass()` — hook that detects glass availability (guards with `Platform.OS === 'ios'`).
- `EtGlassView` — renders native `GlassView` on iOS 26+ or plain `View` elsewhere.
- `LiquidGlassContext` — context provided at root; consumed by subcomponents.
- All from `libs/etoro-ui/src/core/liquid-glass/`.

### Caveats

- **Never set `opacity < 1`** on `EtGlassView` or its parents. Use `animate` and `animationDuration` props for fade effects.
- **`isInteractive` prop** on `GlassView` can only be set once on mount. Remount with a new `key` to toggle.
- Glass wrapping does not affect touch targets — `hitSlop` on `TopbarAction` remains effective.

